# Combinations that work wherever the player happens to be.
#
# Room-scoped combos are the default (using a key on a specific drawer is positional), but
# combining two things in your own hands has nothing to do with which room you're standing in.
# Anything that reads as a portable action belongs here.

use stamp on licence_form
  "I stamp the form as a clerk of this house, in the Harbourmaster's legal absence. It now says I'm fit to sail, in a font nobody can argue with."
  take licence_form
  give licence

# Act III: the Bill of Health is a portable form, so stamping and dating it work anywhere.
use stamp on bill if not bill_stamped
  "I stamp the Bill of Health: HARBOUR OF PORT VELA, in purple, slightly crooked, which is how you know it's real."
  set bill_stamped
  sound chime

use stamp on bill
  "It's stamped. Stamping it twice would look desperate, and Pike can smell desperate."

use calendar_leaf on bill
  "I copy today's date onto the bill in my neatest figures, and pin the leaf behind it as a receipt. Dated. Nobody ever does the dating."
  take calendar_leaf
  set bill_dated
  sound chime

# Act IV: the requisition for Cray's claims book, stamped in the Harbourmaster's absence.
use stamp on requisition if not req_stamped
  "Any clerk of this house may stamp in the Harbourmaster's absence. Tonight the Harbourmaster is very absent. I stamp the requisition: HARBOUR OF PORT VELA, square in the middle of Cray's little cloud."
  set req_stamped
  sound chime

use stamp on requisition
  "It's stamped. Nib only looks for one. Two would make him nervous, and then he might read it."

# The ledger is corrected in the Keel, in front of everyone (rooms_act4.ts); anywhere else, not yet.
use stamp on ledger if not quarantine_lifted
  "Not yet. Until Marta says otherwise, this book is evidence, and you don't stamp evidence. You hold it up."

use stamp on ledger if not ledger_written
  "Not here. An entry like this one wants witnesses, and the Salty Keel is full of them."

use stamp on ledger
  "It's stamped. Once is a correction. Twice is a nervous habit."

combos fill_bucket
  use bucket on lagoon
    "I wade in to the knees and fill the bucket. The lagoon is warm, clear, and entirely unaware it's about to be used as evidence."
    take bucket
    give bucket_water
    sound pickup
  use bucket_water on lagoon
    "It's full. Any fuller and I'd be carrying the lagoon by the handle."

combos quill_combos
  use bill on quill if not bill_signed
    "I hold out the Bill of Health, open at the line marked SHIP'S OFFICER. Quill looks at it, and then at me, and takes the pencil."
    set bill_signed
    talk quill3 at sign
  use bill on quill
    "“I've signed it once, cargo. Twice and it's a habit.”"
  use ansel_log on quill
    "She doesn't open it again. “I've read it. Once was the right number of times.”"
  use crowbar on quill
    "She pushes it back. “I packed it for you. Don't make it a whole thing.”"
  use calendar_leaf on quill
    "“A day. What am I meant to do with a day?” She hands it back. “Put it on the bill, cargo. That's what days are for.”"
  use flag16 on quill
    "She won't take it. “Your father gave it to you. Run it up yourself.”"
  use bucket_water on quill
    "“Throw that at me, cargo, and you'd better be able to swim.”"
  use bucket on quill
    "“That's a bucket. I've seen one. Fill it with something, then we'll talk.”"
  use compass on quill
    "She glances at the needle. “Still pointing at trouble. Good. Keeps things simple.”"
  use stamp on quill
    "She holds out the back of her hand, gravely. I stamp it. She looks at it for longer than a joke needs."
